@@OLD
characters as whitespace through one shared step and takes a value it passes
on from the line as written; and a parse that fails, or a grammar token it
@@NEW
characters as whitespace through one shared step, takes every value it passes
on from the line as written, and never splits such a line by awk's default
field splitting; and a parse that fails, or a grammar token it
@@END
@@OLD
Manifest definitions use the same quoted-content rules as other declarations;
fenced, commented, blockquoted or raw-HTML-hidden examples cannot establish a
prior finding.
@@NEW
Manifest definitions use the same quoted-content rules as other declarations;
fenced, commented, blockquoted or raw-HTML-hidden examples cannot establish a
prior finding. A manifest field line is decided by its label and must be
written `- **Class:**` or `- **Severity:**`, its value the text after that
label only; a finding, a field or a heading the pass cannot read is refused by
name, never dropped.
@@END
